// TEST: Curried Extent Mismatch (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3016
// ============================================================================
// `f(a: T^1, b: T^1) = a + b` co-iterates its two parameters. The call-site
// extent check (BL3016) used to see only `f(a, b)`: a LET-BOUND partial
// application `let h = f(a); h(b)` left `h`'s parameter an open variable, and
// shape monomorphization then typed `b` at `a`'s extent -- the walk read the
// 2-vector past its end (`[5, 7, <garbage>]`), caught only by the runtime
// guard (BL8011) inside the body.
//
// The call judgment instantiates `f`'s signature per call, so `f(a)` teaches
// its OWN copy of `T` from `a`, and the partial application's residual
// parameter is pinned to that instance: `h` takes an `Array<Float64 like
// Idx<3>>`, and `h(b)` is refused at compile time by the same extent rule as
// the direct call. (The runtime guard stays pinned by functions/129 and
// index-types/258, for extents only known at run time.)
function f(a: T^1, b: T^1) = a + b
let a = [1.0, 2.0, 3.0]
let b = [4.0, 5.0]
let h = f(a)
let out = h(b)
